{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-b55243f197c6d6fc8443","statement":"\\lemref{lem:pull} gives\nhomomorphisms\n\n\\begin{equation*}\n\\begin{split}\n&p_\\cT^*\\colon H^{G_\\cO}_*(\\cR)\\to\nH_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*\n\\begin{NB}\n-2\\dim G_\\cO+2\\dim\\bN_\\cO\n\\end{NB}\n}\n(i^{\\prime!}A),\n\\\\\n& p_\\cR^*\\colon H^{G_\\cO}_*(\\cR)\\to\nH_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*}(\\DD A),\n\\end{split}\n\\end{equation*}\n\nwhere $A$ denotes $\\DC_{G_\\cK}\\boxtimes\\CC_\\cR$ for short. Then\n$\\CC_{G_\\cK}\\boxtimes\\DC_\\cR = \\DD A$.\n\nWe compose $i^{\\prime*} \\colon H_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*}(\\DD A)\\to\n    H_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^*(i^{\\prime*}\\DD A)$ with the intersection pairing\nin \\subsecref{subsec:AN}<<ref:subsubsec:c>>, we get\n\n\\begin{equation*}\nH_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*}(i^{\\prime!}A)\n\\otimes H_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*}(\\DD A)\n\\to\nH_{G_\\cO\\times G_\\cO}^{*}(\\DC_{p^{-1}(\\cR\\times\\cR)}).\n\\end{equation*}\n\nThe intersection pairing is defined as $i^{\\prime*}\\DD A = \\DD\n    i^{\\prime!} A$. Thus $p^*$ is the composition of $p_\\cT^*\\otimes\n    i^{\\prime*} p_\\cR^*$ and the intersection pairing.\n\\begin{NB}\nThis is Sasha's original approach.\n\\end{NB}","source_id":"arXiv:1601.03586","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"cb27e6fdc13374131dbc7c0784933708466e49c10c297e84fc229c79762a2122","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 12","ref_key":"","name":"","order":21,"deps":[{"ref":"subsubsec:c","card_id":null,"label":null,"resolved":false,"target":"statement"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03586","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"b2e79974e6e250f264382e70c5d3296d4abfc8d5c86da0ff1e8d9db5aafed33f","line":2981,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-26T15:38:02+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":1014,"math_hints":131}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1601.03586","title":"Towards a mathematical definition of Coulomb branches of $3$-dimensional $\\mathcal N=4$ gauge theories, II","abstract":"Consider the $3$-dimensional $\\mathcal N=4$ supersymmetric gauge theory associated with a compact Lie group $G_c$ and its quaternionic representation $\\mathbf M$. Physicists study its Coulomb branch, which is a noncompact hyper-Kähler manifold with an $\\mathrm{SU}(2)$-action, possibly with singularities. We give a mathematical definition of the Coulomb branch as an affine algebraic variety with $\\mathbb C^\\times$-action when $\\mathbf M$ is of a form $\\mathbf N\\oplus\\mathbf N^*$, as the second step of the proposal given in arXiv:1503.03676.","authors":["Alexander Braverman","Michael Finkelberg","Hiraku Nakajima"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.03586","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"cal":"\\mathcal","Bbb":"\\mathbb","frak":"\\mathfrak","labelenumi":"\\textup{(\\theenumi)}","mathcal":"\\cal","mathbb":"\\Bbb","mathfrak":"\\frak","theenumi":"\\alph{enumi}","thmref":"\\ref{#1}","secref":"\\ref{#1}","lemref":"\\ref{#1}","propref":"\\ref{#1}","corref":"\\ref{#1}","subsecref":"\\ref{#1}","remref":"\\ref{#1}","defeq":"\\overset{\\operatorname{\\scriptstyle def.}}{=}","CC":"{\\mathbb C}","ZZ":"{\\mathbb Z}","QQ":"{\\mathbb Q}","RR":"{\\mathbb R}","proj":"{\\mathbb P}","CP":"\\proj","SL":"\\operatorname{\\rm SL}","SU":"\\operatorname{\\rm SU}","GL":"\\operatorname{GL}","PGL":"\\operatorname{PGL}","U":"\\operatorname{\\rm U}","grpSp":"\\operatorname{\\rm Sp}","algsl":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{sl}}","su":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{su}}","gl":"\\operatorname{\\mathfrak{gl}}","g":"{\\mathfrak g}","Spec":"\\operatorname{Spec}\\nolimits","Proj":"\\operatorname{Proj}\\nolimits","End":"\\operatorname{End}","Hom":"\\operatorname{Hom}","Ker":"\\operatorname{Ker}","Coker":"\\operatorname{Coker}","Ima":"\\operatorname{Im}","dim":"\\mathop{\\text{\\rm dim}}\\nolimits","codim":"\\mathop{\\text{\\